course: dictionary
lesson: 16105
title: One word, two jobs: weeds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do more than one job. The word «weeds» can be a noun, a thing, or a verb, an action. «The old garden was overgrown with weeds.» Here weeds are things: wild plants that grow where people do not want them.
explain: Look at the words around it to find its job. «Every Saturday she weeds the flower bed.» Here she is doing something, so weeds is a verb, and it means she pulls out the wild plants. Ask yourself: is this a thing, or is someone doing something?
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If «pulls out the wild plants» still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Water weeds, also called seaweeds, are a third kind of plant: «Seaweeds grow on the rocks at low tide.»
fact: Weeds are wild plants that grow where people do not want them, such as in gardens, lawns and fields.
fact: Weeds take light, water and space from the plants people want to grow.
fact: «Weeds» can be a verb too: «she weeds the garden» means she pulls out the weeds.
fact: Water weeds, or seaweeds, are plants that grow in water.
fact: One gardener's weed can be useful to wildlife: a dandelion or clover can be food for bees.
exercise: «The old garden was overgrown with weeds.» In this sentence, what are weeds? | Vegetables grown for dinner | Tools for digging | *Wild plants growing where people do not want them | Small grey stones
exercise: «Every Saturday she weeds the flower bed.» What does weeds mean here? | Cuts the hedge | Plants the seeds | Waters the grass | *Pulls out the wild plants
exercise: «Seaweeds grow on the rocks at low tide.» Find and copy the word that means plants that grow in water. | *seaweeds | rocks | tide | grow
test: «She weeds the garden every week.» Is weeds a thing or an action here, and what does it mean? | Thing: a tool for digging | Thing: plants that grow wild | Action: plants new seeds in spring | *Action: pulls out the wild plants
test: Why do gardeners pull up weeds? | Because weeds are always useful to the flowers | Because weeds make the best food for dinner | *Because weeds take light, water and space from the plants they want | Because weeds only grow in the sea
exam: A gardener calls clover a weed, but a wildlife lover leaves it in the lawn. Why? | It is a weed, so it must be left to grow tall | *Bees and other wildlife use it as food | It stops the grass growing at all | It is a kind of seaweed that grows in water
